{
  "info": {
    "name": "FSMS - Feature 10 - Decline Service Request",
    "description": "Feature 10 tests: POST /api/v1/service-requests/:id/decline (roles MANAGER and ADMIN, body: reason).\n\nWHAT THIS ENDPOINT DOES\n- Guards, in order: request exists -> requester is not the customer on the request -> status transition PENDING_REVIEW -> DECLINED is legal.\n- reason is required and validated by zod (trimmed, 1..500 chars, no unknown fields).\n- In ONE transaction: sets ServiceRequest.status = DECLINED and writes AuditLog action REQUEST_DECLINED with metadata { reason }.\n- No WorkOrder is created. There is no declineReason column on ServiceRequest.\n\nBEFORE RUNNING - set these collection variables:\n- baseUrl (default http://localhost:5000)\n- customerToken, technicianToken, managerToken, adminToken (raw JWT values, no 'Bearer ' prefix)\n- serviceId (an active service id whose customer has a complete address)\n- managerOwnRequestId (optional: a request whose customerId equals the manager's userId)\n- adminOwnRequestId (optional: a request whose customerId equals the admin's userId)\n\nHOW TO RUN\n1. Run the 'Setup' folder. It creates fresh PENDING_REVIEW requests as the customer and stores their ids.\n2. Run the 'Decline' folder in order. It covers manager/admin happy paths, missing/empty/unknown reason 400s, repeat-decline 400, invalid-transition 400, 401, wrong-role 403s and 404.\n3. Run the 'Verify' folder to confirm ServiceRequest = DECLINED and no WorkOrder was created.\n4. The 'Self-decline guard' folder only works if you prepare managerOwnRequestId/adminOwnRequestId (see that folder's description).\n\nDB CHECKS (run after declining a request, replacing <REQUEST_ID>):\n  SELECT id, status FROM service_requests WHERE id = '<REQUEST_ID>';\n  SELECT id, status, \"serviceRequestId\" FROM work_orders WHERE \"serviceRequestId\" = '<REQUEST_ID>';\n  SELECT action, \"entityType\", \"entityId\", \"userId\", metadata, \"createdAt\" FROM audit_logs WHERE \"entityId\" = '<REQUEST_ID>' AND action = 'REQUEST_DECLINED';\nExpected: request DECLINED, ZERO work order rows, exactly one REQUEST_DECLINED audit row whose metadata is {\"reason\":\"...\"}.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    { "key": "baseUrl", "value": "http://localhost:5000" },
    { "key": "customerToken", "value": "" },
    { "key": "technicianToken", "value": "" },
    { "key": "managerToken", "value": "" },
    { "key": "adminToken", "value": "" },
    { "key": "serviceId", "value": "" },
    { "key": "reasonText", "value": "Duplicate request - already serviced under ticket 4412" },
    { "key": "managerDeclineRequestId", "value": "" },
    { "key": "adminDeclineRequestId", "value": "" },
    { "key": "missingReasonRequestId", "value": "" },
    { "key": "repeatDeclineRequestId", "value": "" },
    { "key": "invalidTransitionRequestId", "value": "" },
    { "key": "noTokenRequestId", "value": "" },
    { "key": "managerOwnRequestId", "value": "" },
    { "key": "adminOwnRequestId", "value": "" }
  ],
  "item": [
